    },
    {
      "Activity Name": "Summary and Real-world Extension",
      "Duration": "15 minutes",
      "Procedure": "1. Teacher summarizes the core content of the class. 2. Share famous real cases: the 2003 Northeast US blackout and 2008 Toyota acceleration bug were both caused by concurrency errors, ask students to think about how to avoid such problems. 3. Arrange pre-reading for next class: solutions to concurrency problems (mutex, semaphore).",
      "Activity Objective": "Sort out knowledge system, connect theory with real industry cases, arouse interest in follow-up learning"
    },
    {
      "Activity Name": "Q&A",
      "Duration": "10 minutes",
      "Procedure": "Answer students' individual doubts about the content of this class",
      "Activity Objective": "Solve knowledge blind spots in time"
    }
  ],
  "After-class Assessment": [
    "1. Concept question: Briefly explain the difference between concurrency and parallelism, and give one example for each case.",
    "2. Analysis question: If two threads both execute `counter = counter - 1` once on a shared counter with initial value 1, what are the possible final values? Explain the root cause.",
