      "Stimulate scientific interest in addressing unmet clinical needs in cancer therapy"
    ]
  },
  "key_points_and_difficulties": {
    "key_points": [
      "Classification of cancer drug resistance: intrinsic vs acquired resistance",
      "Core mechanisms: ABC transporter-mediated drug efflux, driver gene mutation, epigenetic remodeling, cancer stem cell dormancy, tumor microenvironment-mediated immune tolerance, specific mechanisms of resistance to chemotherapy, targeted therapy and immunotherapy",
      "Mainstream clinical management strategies: dose optimization, sequential therapy, combination therapy, targeted intervention for resistance mutations, and emerging anti-resistance therapies"
    ],
    "difficult_points": [
      "Integrating multiple overlapping resistance mechanisms to develop personalized intervention strategies for individual patients",
      "Understanding the gap between preclinical research findings and clinical translation of anti-resistance therapies, and recognizing current unsolved challenges in the field"
