      "mechanism": "Persistence and effort investment",
      "motivation_link": "Higher self-efficacy predicts greater sustained effort and persistence when facing obstacles or setbacks. People who believe in their ability to succeed maintain motivation through difficulty, while those with low self-efficacy are predisposed to reduce effort or abandon goals early even when they have the actual skill to succeed."
    },
    {
      "mechanism": "Setback attribution",
      "motivation_link": "People with high self-efficacy attribute failures to adjustable factors (poor strategy, insufficient effort) rather than fixed lack of ability, which preserves motivation to adjust approach and continue pursuit. Those with low self-efficacy attribute setbacks to inherent inability, which erodes motivation and leads to disengagement."
    },
    {
      "mechanism": "Affect regulation",
      "motivation_link": "High self-efficacy reduces anticipatory anxiety and fear of failure, allowing motivation to be focused on goal attainment rather than avoiding negative judgment or outcomes. Low self-efficacy increases anxiety that diverts cognitive resources and reduces approach motivation for goal pursuit."
    }
